seoDescription: How a Telegram parsing failure changed the design of my verified 3.19-second inbox triage workflow.
---

The database looked healthy. The two money-related alerts never arrived.

Classification had worked. Extraction had worked. The records existed.

## The failure lived after the database

Telegram rejected the notifications because legacy Markdown treated the underscore in quote_request and invoice_chase as formatting.

The two categories most likely to need human attention were the two categories nobody saw.

## The fix separated storage from delivery

I changed the workflow to use HTML parsing and escaped copies of every field sent to Telegram. Raw email remains untouched in storage.

A regression run included quote_request plus angle brackets and an ampersand in the subject. The alert delivered.

## The routing rules stay explicit

Money and legal language always reach a human. High urgency reaches a human. A draft containing an unresolved price placeholder reaches a human. Malformed model output fails closed.

Spam gets logged, then stays silent.

## Speed is only the visible receipt

Four published executions averaged 3.19 seconds.

The workflow now logs first, routes second and keeps risky messages visible. The tested failure path is the stronger receipt.

Built by handlit.
